<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Everyone signed in to Lanyard can tell the Lanyard team what they think, in two ways. Feedback goes to
        Lanyard's platform admins along with the sender's name and the page they were on. Neither appears for
        visitors to the public demo.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The feedback button">
        <ol>
            <li>Press the <strong>Send feedback</strong> button (a person with a speech bubble) in the top bar, on any page.</li>
            <li>Choose <strong>Good</strong> or <strong>Not great</strong>.</li>
            <li>Add a comment if you like. It's optional, and can be up to 2,000 characters.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Send feedback</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <HelpNote>
            So a stuck finger can't fill the inbox, one person can send up to 10 pieces of feedback an hour.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="The star rating prompt">
        <FluentText>
            Now and then, "How would you rate Lanyard?" appears in the bottom corner, about 20 seconds after a page
            opens. Pick 1 to 5 stars, say what the main reason for your score is if you like, and press
            <strong>Send</strong>.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>It isn't shown in someone's first week, or on the sign-in, account, clock-in scan or feedback pages.</li>
            <li>After you've sent a rating, you won't be asked again for 30 days.</li>
            <li><strong>Not now</strong> (or the close button, or Escape) puts it off for a week. Ignoring it does the same.</li>
            <li><strong>Don't ask again</strong> stops it for good. You can still use the feedback button.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
